{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Point-Line-Curve Hierarchy.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Point-Line-Curve Hierarchy.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"point line curve hierarchy point line curve hierarchy","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Point-Line-Curve Hierarchy.md","fileName":"Point-Line-Curve Hierarchy.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Point-Line-Curve Hierarchy","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 00:45\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Engineering Geometry Foundations]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Engineering Geometry Foundations","geometrycreationandimport.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Point-Line-Curve Hierarchy.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Point-Line-Curve Hierarchy.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"point line curve hierarchy point line curve hierarchy","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Point-Line-Curve Hierarchy.md","fileName":"Point-Line-Curve Hierarchy.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Point-Line-Curve Hierarchy","heading":"Point-Line-Curve Hierarchy","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A point marks a location without length, a line connects locations along a straight one-dimensional path, and a curve generalizes that path by allowing its direction to vary. Endpoints and intersections create the vertices through which these entities connect.\n\nIn a model, the hierarchy is operational as well as descriptive. Points can receive concentrated conditions, lines can carry one-dimensional physics or bound faces, and curves can represent edges whose continuity and curvature affect meshing.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Engineering Geometry Foundations","geometrycreationandimport.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Point-Line-Curve Hierarchy.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Fu